- How would you recover the exact endpoints from the DP table?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests DP over partitioning with an order-dependent gain, plus reconstruction. Distinct from standard sum-of-maximums or cooldown problems.

## Key Concepts

- Order-dependent block weighting
- Prefix sums for O(1) subarray sums
- 2D DP with backtracking pointers
- Time/space trade-offs and reconstruction

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxValue(A, k) {
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const dp = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({ length: n+1 }, () => Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++) {
      // end a block at i
      for (let j = 0; j <= i; j++) {
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + (pref[i+1] - pref[j]) * t;
        if (val > dp[i+1][t]) {
          dp[i+1][t] = val;
          par[i+1][t] = j;
        }
      }
      // skip i is implicit via dp[i+1][t] initialization from dp[i][t]
      if (dp[i][t] > dp[i+1][t]) {
        dp[i+1][t] = dp[i][t];
        par[i+1][t] = -2; // indicate skip
      }
    }
  }
  // Reconstruction omitted for brevity
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to optimize to near O(nk) for special A (e.g., non-decreasing) or under additional constraints?
- How would you extend to allow at most k blocks or to recover the exact endpoints efficiently?

## Why This Is Asked

This question tests a concrete DP pattern for selecting exactly k non-overlapping subarrays with a fixed per-subarray cost. It requires careful state definitions, reconstruction, and edge-case handling of negative sums.

## Key Concepts

- DP for k disjoint subarrays with end-state tracking
- Prefix sums or running sums to compute subarray value fast
- Reconstruction pointers to recover endpoints
- Time: O(nk); Space: O(nk) (with optimizations)

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxKSubarrays(A, k, c) {
  const n = A.length, NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const end = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) {
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++) {
      end[i][t] = NEG;
      if (t > 0) end[i][t] = Math.max(end[i-1][t] + A[i-1], dp[i-1][t-1] + A[i-1] - c);
      dp[i][t] = Math.max(dp[i-1][t], end[i][t]);
    }
  }
  return dp[n][k];
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How to optimize to O(nk) time and O(k) space?
- How handle cases where all values are negative or c is large?

## Why This Is Asked
This question tests building a DP over subsequences with constraints, requiring a clear state definition and transition over previous indices, plus reconstruction capabilities.

## Key Concepts
- Subsequence DP with constraints
- State dp[i] and parent tracking
- Time/space analysis and reconstruction

## Code Example
```javascript
function maxSubseqWithDiff(a, d) {
  const n = a.length;
  const dp = Array(n).fill(0);
  const par = Array(n).fill(-1);
  let best = -Infinity, bestIdx = -1;

  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) {
    dp[i] = a[i];
    for (let j = 0; j < i; j++) {
      if (Math.abs(a[i] - a[j]) <= d && dp[j] + a[i] > dp[i]) {
        dp[i] = dp[j] + a[i];
        par[i] = j;
      }
    }
    if (dp[i] > best) {
      best = dp[i];
      bestIdx = i;
    }
  }

  // Reconstruct subsequence
  const seq = [];
  let curr = bestIdx;
  while (curr !== -1) {
    seq.push(curr);
    curr = par[curr];
  }
  return { maxSum: best, subsequence: seq.reverse() };
}
```

## Time/Space Complexity
Time: O(n²) due to nested loops checking all previous indices
Space: O(n) for dp and parent arrays

## Why This Is Asked
This question introduces a new DP angle: partitioning a string into k segments with a per-segment distinct-character score, a practical proxy for text analytics. It tests state formulation, precomputation, and reconstruction, with a baseline O(n^2k) DP suitable for beginner to intermediate levels.

## Key Concepts
- DP on partitioning problems
- Precomputing substring properties in O(n^2)
- Reconstructing cuts via parent pointers

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxScorePartition(s, k){
  const n = s.length;
  const dist = Array.from({length:n}, ()=> Array(n).fill(0));
  for(let i=0;i<n;i++){
    const seen = new Set();
    for(let j=i;j<n;j++){
      seen.add(s[j]);
      dist[i][j] = seen.size;
    }
  }
  const dp = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const par = Array.from({length:n+1}, ()=> Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  for(let i=1;i<=n;i++){
    for(let t=1;t<=Math.min(i,k);t++){
      for(let j=t-1;j<=i-1;j++){
        const val = dp[j][t-1] + dist[j][i-1];
        if(val > dp[i][t]){ dp[i][t] = val; par[i][t] = j; }
      }
    }
  }
  // reconstruction could be added here
  return {score: dp[n][k], cutStartIndices: []};
}
```

